    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44844" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔπους</span></b> , ὁ, ἡ, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πουν</span>, τό, gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποδος</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with good feet</i>, of
			horses and dogs, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				1.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				3.2
			</span></i>; of a bird, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔπους καὶ κακόπτερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					617b4
				</span></i>
			; <i>fleet of foot</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δηωΐνη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					48
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>with good feet, flowing</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁρμονία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					6.54
				</span></i>
			 (Paul. Sil.).</div>
